6445409 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445409 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186445398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445409 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "ce961bdb-0b16-58aa-9186-57cb2f2ecbd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445406 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-186817" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445410 #edb/ref 1071 "$-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "04148a8c-1c50-5c75-a5ce-265853c3b05d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445410 #edb/ref 1074 "We put both fractions over a common denominator of $15$ and then add the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{9}{15}=\\frac{-7+9}{15}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $9$ to $-7,$ we start at $-7$ on a number line and move $9$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/f2/f2d170548e38956afa1354e7df74f645ea5101c3dde6665c110ada01ab7a96b8.png)\n\nSo, $-7+9=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+9}{15}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{-7+9}{15}=\\frac{9-7}{15}=\\frac{2}{15}.\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\frac{7}{15}+\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{2}{15}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445411 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445407 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445411 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42771" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445411 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445411 #edb/ref 1071 "$-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445411 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2f37489a-3f1a-5d45-bf2c-50769e7aa76a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445411 #edb/ref 1074 "Since both fractions have a common denominator of $6$, we can combine them to form one fraction, which gives\n \n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{-1+5}{6}.\n$$\n\nTo compute the numerator, we can use either Method 1 or Method 2, shown below.\n\n**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $5$ to $-1,$ we start at $-1$ on a number line and move $5$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/63/632e4bcce5b619f9a5c4dfb2c414a33da0e9567b7b4d8b15adb439da1b3dd88d.png)\n\nSo, $-1+5=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{-1+5}{6}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers in the numerator, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-1+5}{6}=\\frac{5-1}{6}=\\frac{4}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we conclude that $-\\frac{1}{6}+\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{2}{3}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445412 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445409 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445412 #edb/ref 1069 "q-186761" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445412 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445412 #edb/ref 1071 "$-4+1.3=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445412 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "456bbb28-9f6e-59b4-94a9-4565fc858899" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445412 #edb/ref 1074 "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-4+1.3=1.3-4=-2.7\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445413 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445404 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445413 #edb/ref 1069 "q-171019" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445413 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445413 #edb/ref 1071 "$-5.1+7.8=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445413 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b19e586f-b5e5-54ad-9f34-9f32c29b74be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445413 #edb/ref 1074 "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-5.1+7.8=7.8-5.1=2.7\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445414 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445405 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445414 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2111" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445414 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445414 #edb/ref 1071 "$-2+4=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445414 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d61e161d-c16f-54c4-b847-5ce2fd8181a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445414 #edb/ref 1074 "**Method 1 - Picturing a Number Line**\n\nTo add $4$ to $-2,$ we start at $-2$ on a number line and move $4$ spaces to the right.\n\n![](images/29/291bb445c414ae60c0093038554a780370b3e4d747e7e51a737aa15ffa7a6cf0.png)\n\nWe end up at $2.$ So, $-2+4=2.$\n\n**Method 2 - Subtraction in Reverse**\n\nWe can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-2+4=4-2=2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445415 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186445408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445415 #edb/ref 1069 "q-186759" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445415 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445415 #edb/ref 1071 "$-7.2+9=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445415 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dbe692b7-3891-54fa-af44-56909b7f8af6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186445415 #edb/ref 1074 "We can swap the order of the numbers and then compute the resulting subtraction:\n\n$$\n-7.2+9=9-7.2=1.8\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
